<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
                            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
        Stores (echno-backend #914): materials, site transfers, stock adjustments and the stock ledger.
        Today the four are guarded differently, and the one inventory area of the template would widen
        some of them:

        - Stock adjustments: the system admin, project manager and store keeper read, raise and edit
          one; the system admin and project manager approve, reject and delete it. That is the
          template's inventory area as it stands, so it keeps the name.
        - The ledger: the same three read the movements behind a material, location, project or task,
          but only the system admin and store keeper list it over the whole organization (all, paged,
          by type, by date range). That one read differs, so it is the named action
          inventory:read-ledger.
        - Materials: the three read the catalogue, the system admin and project manager create and edit
          it, the system admin alone deletes a material or removes a threshold override, and all three
          set a reorder threshold at a storage location. Create, edit and delete differ from
          inventory, so materials become an area of their own, with materials:set-thresholds for the
          one write the store keeper holds.
        - Site transfers: the three read, and only the system admin and store keeper raise, receive,
          cancel or move one. Create and edit differ from inventory, so site transfers become an area
          of their own.

        Nothing is deleted: the project manager's inventory create, edit, approve and delete and the
        store keeper's inventory create and edit are all used by stock adjustments.

        A file of its own because 008 loads role-template-grants.csv with no runOnChange. The
        reconciler carries the template to every uncustomized role on the next boot, in both
        directions; a customized role is left as its organization set it.
    -->

    <changeSet id="access-015-stores" author="abhijith">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <sqlCheck expectedResult="0">
                SELECT count(*) FROM access_role_template_grant
                WHERE template_id = 'ed34dfe6-5468-5f6e-b6ed-ef6eefccfce2'
                  AND permission_key = 'materials:read'
            </sqlCheck>
        </preConditions>
        <loadData tableName="access_role_template_grant" file="db/data/access/role-template-grants-stores.csv" separator=",">
            <column name="id" type="UUID"/>
            <column name="template_id" type="UUID"/>
            <column name="permission_key" type="STRING"/>
            <column name="scope" type="STRING"/>
        </loadData>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
